### =======================================================================
### Hitorro Mesh — runnable HTTP recipes
###
### Open this file in IntelliJ (Ultimate, or Community with the HTTP Client
### plugin). A green "run" arrow appears in the gutter next to every `###`
### block. Click to run, response shows in the tool window.
###
### Prereqs — start the mesh once, then run any of these repeatedly:
###
###   cd hitorro-mesh-examples/scripts
###   ./mesh-init-data.sh   # writes sample data + configs
###   ./mesh-up.sh          # boots nats + driver + 2 agents
###
### Tear down when done:
###
###   ./mesh-down.sh
###
### Switch the target driver by picking an environment (IntelliJ shows a
### dropdown at the top-right of the editor). See http-client.env.json
### in this directory.
### =======================================================================

@driverHost = http://localhost:8085


### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Section 1 — Cluster inspection (start here to confirm the mesh is up)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### GetAgents — should return at least one live jvssql-capable agent
GET {{driverHost}}/mesh/agents

> {%
    client.test("at least one agent live", () => {
        client.assert(response.body.length >= 1, "no agents heartbeating");
    });
    client.global.set("firstAgentId", response.body[0].agentId);
%}

### GetTables — see which distributed + broadcast tables are registered
GET {{driverHost}}/mesh/tables

### GetCluster — merged view of declared vs live agents (HEALTHY/MISSING/ORPHAN)
GET {{driverHost}}/mesh/cluster

### CompositeHealth — includes the MeshHealthIndicator with per-partition coverage
GET {{driverHost}}/actuator/health

### MeshHealthIndicatorAlone — just the mesh's status
GET {{driverHost}}/actuator/health/mesh

### LivenessProbe — Spring built-in; JVM-only; use for K8s livenessProbe
GET {{driverHost}}/actuator/health/liveness

### PrometheusScrape — all `mesh_*` meters + JVM + HTTP
GET {{driverHost}}/actuator/prometheus


### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Section 2 — Basic batch queries
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### FilterProjection — SELECT with WHERE, results collected then returned
POST {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "SELECT id, title FROM docs WHERE lang = 'en'",
  "timeoutMs": 5000
}

> {%
    client.test("returned rows", () => {
        client.assert(response.body.rowCount > 0, "no rows returned");
    });
    client.test("not timed out", () => {
        client.assert(response.body.timedOut === false);
    });
%}

### GroupByCount — distributed aggregate with combiner-at-driver (phase 2)
POST {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "SELECT lang, COUNT(*) AS n FROM docs GROUP BY lang",
  "timeoutMs": 5000
}

### GroupByAvg — AVG decomposes to SUM+COUNT partials, driver reconstructs
POST {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "SELECT lang, AVG(size_kb) AS avg_size FROM docs GROUP BY lang",
  "timeoutMs": 5000
}

### DistinctRewrite — SELECT DISTINCT auto-rewrites to GROUP BY <all cols>
POST {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "SELECT DISTINCT lang FROM docs",
  "timeoutMs": 5000
}

### HavingFilter — HAVING clause on aggregate result
POST {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "SELECT lang, COUNT(*) AS n FROM docs GROUP BY lang HAVING n >= 1",
  "timeoutMs": 5000
}

### OrderByLimit — LIMIT pushed down to agents (phase 5b.3); N-way merge sort at driver
POST {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "SELECT id, size_kb FROM docs ORDER BY size_kb DESC LIMIT 5",
  "timeoutMs": 5000
}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Section 3 — Query planning + debugging
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### ExplainSimple — see the plan the mesh picks (no execution)
GET {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries/explain?sql=SELECT+id+FROM+docs+WHERE+lang%3D%27en%27

### ExplainAggregate — TwoStagePlan with partial + combine SQL visible
GET {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries/explain?sql=SELECT+lang%2C+COUNT%28*%29+FROM+docs+GROUP+BY+lang

### ExplainAggregateAliased — verify AS aliases preserved in combine SQL
GET {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries/explain?sql=SELECT+lang+AS+language%2C+COUNT%28*%29+AS+total+FROM+docs+GROUP+BY+lang


### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Section 4 — Query lifecycle: retries, timeouts, cancellation
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### RetryOnFailure — whole-query retry with exponential backoff (phase 7g)
### Response `attempts` field shows how many were needed.
POST {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "SELECT id FROM docs WHERE lang = 'en'",
  "timeoutMs": 5000,
  "retries": 2
}

### ShortTimeout — deadline fires before completion → timedOut: true, 200 OK
### with whatever rows arrived before deadline (may be empty).
POST {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "SELECT id FROM docs",
  "timeoutMs": 1
}

> {%
    // Very-short timeout — expect either a full result (fast mesh) or
    // timedOut:true (deadline fired). Both are correct.
    client.test("response either completed OR timedOut", () => {
        client.assert(response.status === 200);
    });
%}

### ListActiveQueries — while a long query runs, see it here (phase 7d)
GET {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries

### CancelUnknownQuery — DELETE with unknown queryId returns 400 (idempotent)
DELETE {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries/does-not-exist

> {%
    client.test("unknown queryId → 400", () => {
        client.assert(response.status === 400);
        client.assert(response.body.error === "bad_request");
    });
%}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Section 5 — SSE (streaming results row-by-row)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### StreamAsSSE — server pushes one event per row, then a `complete` event
### IntelliJ's HTTP Client renders each SSE event as it arrives.
GET {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries/stream?sql=SELECT+id+FROM+docs+WHERE+lang%3D%27en%27&timeoutMs=30000
Accept: text/event-stream


### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Section 6 — Structured error responses (phase 7c)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### BadSql — unregistered table → 400 with `error: bad_request`
POST {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "SELECT id FROM does_not_exist",
  "timeoutMs": 5000
}

> {%
    client.test("bad table → 400", () => {
        client.assert(response.status === 400);
    });
%}

### JoinAgainstUnregistered — non-broadcast JOIN → 400 with actionable message
POST {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "SELECT d.id, x.y FROM docs d JOIN x ON d.id = x.did",
  "timeoutMs": 5000
}

> {%
    client.test("non-broadcast JOIN → 400", () => {
        client.assert(response.status === 400);
        client.assert(response.body.message.includes("broadcast"));
    });
%}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Section 7 — Broadcast JOIN (only if `langs` broadcast table is registered)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### To enable these, add to driver.yml:
###   broadcast-tables: [langs]
### And every agent's config:
###   broadcast-tables:
###     - name: langs
###       type-json-resource: file:/path/to/langs.json
###       ndjson-file: file:/path/to/langs.ndjson

### BroadcastInnerJoin — docs INNER JOIN langs (phase 4a)
POST {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "SELECT d.id, l.name FROM docs d JOIN langs l ON d.lang = l.code",
  "timeoutMs": 5000
}

### BroadcastLeftOuter — unmatched left rows null-padded (phase 4c)
POST {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "SELECT d.id, l.name FROM docs d LEFT JOIN langs l ON d.lang = l.code",
  "timeoutMs": 5000
}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Section 8 — Shuffle-hash JOIN (needs `events` distributed table)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Register `events` as a second distributed table on the driver + host
### its partitions on their respective agents.

### ShuffleInnerJoin — fact × fact join (phase 4b)
POST {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "SELECT d.id, e.action FROM docs d JOIN events e ON d.id = e.doc_id",
  "timeoutMs": 15000
}

### ShufflePlusWhere — WHERE conjuncts push down to per-side scans (phase 4b.2.1)
POST {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "SELECT d.id, e.action FROM docs d JOIN events e ON d.id = e.doc_id WHERE d.lang = 'en' AND e.action = 'view'",
  "timeoutMs": 15000
}

### ShufflePlusGroupBy — three-stage combine (phase 4b.2)
POST {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sql": "SELECT d.lang, COUNT(*) AS interactions FROM docs d JOIN events e ON d.id = e.doc_id GROUP BY d.lang",
  "timeoutMs": 15000
}


### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Section 9 — Streaming windowed aggregate (needs streaming source registered)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Requires an agent registered with a streaming table (Kafka / NATS
### JetStream / InMemoryStreamingTable). See phase 6d.1/6d.2 in
### ROADMAP.md for setup.

### WindowedStreamingSSE — long-lived query; per-window rows arrive as SSE events
### Cancel via DELETE with the queryId from the `opened` event.
GET {{driverHost}}/mesh/queries/stream?sql=SELECT+WIN_START%28event_time%2C+60000%29+AS+ws%2C+COUNT%28*%29+AS+n+FROM+events+GROUP+BY+WIN_START%28event_time%2C+60000%29&timeoutMs=3600000
Accept: text/event-stream


